  "formal_relation": {
    "prompt": "/no_think\nFor every supplied pair, return exactly one outcome: no_relation, contains, prerequisite, or related. contains means source is the broader whole and target is its component. prerequisite means learners should understand source before target for concrete learning reasons; page order or adjacency alone is never proof. related requires a specific meaningful learning association and is never an uncertainty fallback. Use no_relation when the grounded content does not establish one of the three relations. Retrieval signals are hints only. Cite only supplied Claim, Evidence, and context aliases; use document_structure or combined only with context refs. Give a concise learner-readable reason that states the actual learning semantics. Set needs_review when support is indirect, conflicting, or limited. Return every pair id exactly once as JSON and no extra fields.",
